WEBVTT

00:35:59.770 --> 00:36:01.587
AG: When I went through this exercise,

00:36:01.611 --> 00:36:03.557
I started thinking about silver linings,

00:36:03.581 --> 00:36:06.356
aspects of being fully remote
that I'll miss,

00:36:06.380 --> 00:36:09.156
like having more family time
and flex time,

00:36:09.180 --> 00:36:11.326
not having to travel or commute,

00:36:11.350 --> 00:36:13.526
not having to change out of pajamas

00:36:13.550 --> 00:36:15.202
or at least pajama bottoms.

00:36:16.202 --> 00:36:18.726
Psychologists find that imagining
these silver linings

00:36:18.750 --> 00:36:19.900
fading in the future

00:36:19.924 --> 00:36:21.526
makes them feel scarce.

00:36:21.550 --> 00:36:24.576
That helps us appreciate
them more in the present.

00:36:24.600 --> 00:36:28.236
Next, you can direct
your mental DeLorean to the past.

00:36:28.260 --> 00:36:31.436
This is something Scott has been doing
during the current crisis: